import GX.Topology.Portly

/-!
# Spreads, the ordinary locus, and the partial-covering lemma (§3.1)

The preliminaries on spreads of `papers/gx` (`RamcovGX.tex:822–902`).

* **`def:category_spreads`** — `RamcovGX.tex:825`: `GX.IsSpread` (with `GX.spreadBasis`,
  characterised by `GX.isSpread_iff`), the category `GX.Spread` with morphisms `GX.Spread.Hom`.
* **`rem:spread_open_respectively_co`** — `RamcovGX.tex:835`: `GX.IsSpread.restrict`.
* **`def:continuous_map_ordinary_locus`** — `RamcovGX.tex:838`: `GX.IsEvenlyCoveredSet`,
  `GX.ordY`, `GX.ordX`.
* `rem:ordinary_locii_open_but` — `RamcovGX.tex:843` — partial (a reading of "covering"):
  `GX.isOpen_ordY`, `GX.isOpen_ordX`; not connected: `GX.not_isPreconnected_ordY_abs`,
  `GX.not_isPreconnected_ordX_abs`; covering: `GX.isCoveringMapOn_ordY`,
  `GX.isCoveringMap_restrict_ordX`; the surjectivity caveat `GX.unitTrue_counterexample`.
* **`rem:singular_on_singular`** — `RamcovGX.tex:846`: `GX.image_compl_ordX`.
* **`lem:spread_partial_covering`** — `RamcovGX.tex:851`: `GX.spread_partial_covering`.
* `cex:openess` — `RamcovGX.tex:870` — partial (false as written): `GX.cex_openess`,
  `GX.ordY_lineIncl`.
* `cex:portlyness` — `RamcovGX.tex:874` — partial: item 1 `GX.notMem_ordX_of_notMem_interior`;
  item 2 false as written (`GX.ordY_portlyInv_nonempty`), replaced by `GX.cex_portlyness`.
* **`lem:ord_iso`** — `RamcovGX.tex:889`: `GX.Spread.ord_iso`, general form
  `GX.image_ordX_of_homeomorph`, `GX.image_ordY_of_homeomorph`.

> A spread $X\xrightarrow{p} Y$ is a continuous map such that the topology of $X$ is generated by
> the connected components of the preimages of open subsets of $Y$. […] morphisms […] are couples
> of continuous functions $(f,g)$ such that the following diagram commutes.
>
> Let $X\xrightarrow{p} Y$ be a spread, with $\U,\V$ open of $X$ and $Y$ respectively such that
> $p(\U)\subset \V$, the (co)restriction $p_{|\U}^{|\V}$ is a spread.
>
> Let $X\xrightarrow{p} Y$ be a continuous map, the ordinary locus $\ord_p(Y)$ of $Y$ is the set
> of point $y\in Y$ for which there exists an open neighborhood $\U$ evenly covered by $p$ ie such
> that $p$ maps each connected component of $p^{-1}(\U)$ homeomorphically onto $\U$. The ordinary
> locus $\ord_p(X)$ of $X$ is the preimage of the ordinary locus of $Y$.
>
> The ordinary locii are open but may not be connected. The only obstruction for the restriction
> $\ord(X)\rightarrow \ord(Y)$ to be a covering is the connectedness of $\ord(X)$.
>
> Let $X\xrightarrow{p}Y$ be a surjective continuous map. Then
> $p(X\setminus \ord(X)) = Y\setminus \ord(Y)$.
>
> Let $X\xrightarrow{p} Y$ be a continuous map inducing a covering $X_1\rightarrow Y_1$ for some
> $X_1\subset X$ and $Y_1\subset Y$ with $X_1$ portly and $Y_1$ open. Then $Y_1\subset \ord(Y)$,
> $X_1 \subset \ord(X)$ and $p^{-1}(Y_1)=X_1$.
>
> Consider $X = \RR\times \{0\}$ and $Y = \RR^2$ with $p$ the inclusion map. […] induces a
> covering $X\rightarrow X \subset Y$ but $\ord(Y)=\emptyset$.
>
> If $X_1$ is not open, […] $p$ is not injective in any neighborhood of $x$. In particular,
> $p(x)\notin \ord(Y)$ and $x\notin \ord(X)$. […] However, $\ord(Y)=\emptyset$ since […]
>
> Let $X_i\xrightarrow{p_i} Y_i$ be spreads […] and let $(f,g)$ be a spread isomorphism […].
> Then $g(\ord(X_1)) = \ord(X_2)$ and $f(\ord(Y_1)) = \ord(Y_2)$.

## Hypothesis checklist

| paper hypothesis | here |
|---|---|
| §3 standing: spaces Hausdorff, locally path-connected, first countable | ⚠ weakened: each theorem carries what it uses (`T2Space X`, `LocallyConnectedSpace X`) |
| `rem:spread_open_respectively_co`: `V` open | ⚠ weakened: not used |
| `rem:ordinary_locii_open_but`: (covering part) `X` locally path-connected | ✓ carried as `LocallyConnectedSpace X` (standing hypothesis) |
| `rem:singular_on_singular`: `p` continuous | ⚠ weakened: not used |
| `lem:spread_partial_covering`: `X` Hausdorff, locally path-connected | ✓ carried (`T2Space X`, `LocallyConnectedSpace X`) |
| `lem:spread_partial_covering`: `Y` Hausdorff, locally path-connected, first countable | ⚠ weakened: not used |
| `lem:spread_partial_covering`: "covering `X₁ → Y₁`" | ⚠ weakened: mathlib's `IsCoveringMap` (no surjectivity, no connectedness) |
| `lem:ord_iso`: `p₁`, `p₂` spreads | ⚠ weakened: any maps; only the homeomorphisms and `p₂ ∘ g = f ∘ p₁` are used |

## SCOPE (disclosed)

* "Generated by" is `TopologicalSpace.generateFrom`; the components then form a basis
  (`GX.IsSpread.isTopologicalBasis`) and the source is locally connected
  (`GX.IsSpread.locallyConnectedSpace`). The objects of `GX.Spread` have source and target in one
  universe.
* "Evenly covered" is read literally: a set with empty preimage is evenly covered, so every
  point off `closure (p X)` is ordinary (`GX.compl_closure_range_subset_ordY`). This reading is what
  makes the two "`ord(Y) = ∅`" of the counterexamples false.
* `rem:ordinary_locii_open_but`: "covering" is read as mathlib's `IsCoveringMap`; with it the
  restriction is a covering whether or not `ord(X)` is connected. If "covering" includes
  surjectivity the remark fails (`GX.unitTrue_counterexample`), and holds for a surjective `p`
  (`GX.surjective_restrict_ordX`).
* `cex:openess`: `ord(Y) = ∅` is false; `ord(Y) = Y ∖ p(X)`, `ord(X) = ∅` and `Y₁ ∩ ord(Y) = ∅`.
* `cex:portlyness`, item 2: the paper's `X` with "the coarsest topology making the injection a
  spread" is not built. Whatever its topology, `ord(Y)` contains the open unit disc
  (`GX.ball_subset_ordY_portlyInv`), so `ord(Y) = ∅` is false. The counterexample is
  `GX.cex_portlyness` (`x ↦ ||x| - 1|` on `ℝ`), with every property the paper lists.

Provenance: mathlib `fabf563a` (tag `v4.31.0`), pinned via `lakefile.toml`.
-/

noncomputable section

open Set Filter Topology Function

namespace GX

universe u

variable {X Y : Type*} [TopologicalSpace X] [TopologicalSpace Y]

/-! ### Spreads -/

/-- The connected components of the preimages of open subsets of `Y`. -/
def spreadBasis (p : X → Y) : Set (Set X) :=
  {V | ∃ U : Set Y, IsOpen U ∧ ∃ x ∈ p ⁻¹' U, V = connectedComponentIn (p ⁻¹' U) x}

/-- `def:category_spreads`. A spread is a continuous map such that the topology of the source
is generated by the connected components of the preimages of open subsets of the target. -/
structure IsSpread (p : X → Y) : Prop where
  continuous : Continuous p
  eq_generateFrom : ‹TopologicalSpace X› = TopologicalSpace.generateFrom (spreadBasis p)

theorem isSpread_iff {p : X → Y} :
    IsSpread p ↔ Continuous p ∧ (∀ V ∈ spreadBasis p, IsOpen V) ∧
      ∀ x : X, ∀ O : Set X, IsOpen O → x ∈ O →
        ∃ U : Set Y, IsOpen U ∧ p x ∈ U ∧ connectedComponentIn (p ⁻¹' U) x ⊆ O := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨hc, heq⟩
    refine ⟨hc, fun V hV => ?_, ?_⟩
    · rw [heq]; exact TopologicalSpace.isOpen_generateFrom_of_mem hV
    · intro x O hO hxO
      rw [heq] at hO
      induction hO generalizing x with
      | basic s hs =>
        obtain ⟨U, hU, x₀, hx₀, rfl⟩ := hs
        refine ⟨U, hU, show p x ∈ U from connectedComponentIn_subset (p ⁻¹' U) x₀ hxO, ?_⟩
        rw [connectedComponentIn_eq hxO]
      | univ => exact ⟨univ, isOpen_univ, mem_univ _, subset_univ _⟩
      | inter s t _ _ ihs iht =>
        obtain ⟨U₁, hU₁, hx₁, h₁⟩ := ihs x hxO.1
        obtain ⟨U₂, hU₂, hx₂, h₂⟩ := iht x hxO.2
        refine ⟨U₁ ∩ U₂, hU₁.inter hU₂, ⟨hx₁, hx₂⟩, subset_inter ?_ ?_⟩
        · exact (connectedComponentIn_mono x (preimage_mono inter_subset_left)).trans h₁
        · exact (connectedComponentIn_mono x (preimage_mono inter_subset_right)).trans h₂
      | sUnion S _ ih =>
        obtain ⟨s, hsS, hxs⟩ := mem_sUnion.1 hxO
        obtain ⟨U, hU, hxU, h⟩ := ih s hsS x hxs
        exact ⟨U, hU, hxU, h.trans (subset_sUnion_of_mem hsS)⟩
  · rintro ⟨hc, hopen, hnhds⟩
    refine ⟨hc, ?_⟩
    refine (TopologicalSpace.isTopologicalBasis_of_isOpen_of_nhds hopen ?_).eq_generateFrom
    intro a O haO hO
    obtain ⟨U, hU, haU, h⟩ := hnhds a O hO haO
    exact ⟨_, ⟨U, hU, a, haU, rfl⟩, mem_connectedComponentIn haU, h⟩

/-- Over a locally connected source, the components are automatically open. -/
theorem isSpread_iff_of_locallyConnectedSpace [LocallyConnectedSpace X] {p : X → Y} :
    IsSpread p ↔ Continuous p ∧
      ∀ x : X, ∀ O : Set X, IsOpen O → x ∈ O →
        ∃ U : Set Y, IsOpen U ∧ p x ∈ U ∧ connectedComponentIn (p ⁻¹' U) x ⊆ O := by
  rw [isSpread_iff]
  refine ⟨fun h => ⟨h.1, h.2.2⟩, fun h => ⟨h.1, ?_, h.2⟩⟩
  rintro V ⟨U, hU, x, -, rfl⟩
  exact (hU.preimage h.1).connectedComponentIn

/-- The components of preimages of open sets form a basis of the topology of a spread. -/
theorem IsSpread.isTopologicalBasis {p : X → Y} (hp : IsSpread p) :
    TopologicalSpace.IsTopologicalBasis (spreadBasis p) := by
  obtain ⟨-, hopen, hnhds⟩ := isSpread_iff.1 hp
  refine TopologicalSpace.isTopologicalBasis_of_isOpen_of_nhds hopen ?_
  intro a O haO hO
  obtain ⟨U, hU, haU, h⟩ := hnhds a O hO haO
  exact ⟨_, ⟨U, hU, a, haU, rfl⟩, mem_connectedComponentIn haU, h⟩

/-- The source of a spread is locally connected. -/
theorem IsSpread.locallyConnectedSpace {p : X → Y} (hp : IsSpread p) :
    LocallyConnectedSpace X := by
  obtain ⟨-, hopen, hnhds⟩ := isSpread_iff.1 hp
  rw [locallyConnectedSpace_iff_subsets_isOpen_isConnected]
  intro x O hO
  obtain ⟨O', hO'O, hO', hxO'⟩ := mem_nhds_iff.1 hO
  obtain ⟨U, hU, hxU, h⟩ := hnhds x O' hO' hxO'
  exact ⟨_, h.trans hO'O, hopen _ ⟨U, hU, x, hxU, rfl⟩,
    mem_connectedComponentIn hxU, isConnected_connectedComponentIn_iff.2 hxU⟩

/-- An inducing map with a locally connected source is a spread (e.g. a subspace inclusion). -/
theorem IsSpread.of_isInducing [LocallyConnectedSpace X] {p : X → Y} (hp : IsInducing p) :
    IsSpread p := by
  refine isSpread_iff_of_locallyConnectedSpace.2 ⟨hp.continuous, ?_⟩
  intro x O hO hxO
  obtain ⟨U, hU, rfl⟩ := hp.isOpen_iff.1 hO
  exact ⟨U, hU, hxO, connectedComponentIn_subset _ _⟩

/-- `rem:spread_open_respectively_co`. The (co)restriction of a spread to an open `U ⊆ X` and
any `V ⊆ Y` with `p(U) ⊆ V` is a spread. (The paper takes `V` open; this is not used.) -/
theorem IsSpread.restrict {p : X → Y} (hp : IsSpread p) {U : Set X} {V : Set Y} (hU : IsOpen U)
    (h : MapsTo p U V) : IsSpread (h.restrict p U V) := by
  haveI := hp.locallyConnectedSpace
  haveI : LocallyConnectedSpace U := hU.locallyConnectedSpace
  have hc : Continuous (h.restrict p U V) := hp.continuous.restrict h
  refine isSpread_iff_of_locallyConnectedSpace.2 ⟨hc, ?_⟩
  intro x O hO hxO
  obtain ⟨W, hW, hxW, hWO⟩ := (isSpread_iff.1 hp).2.2 x ((↑) '' O)
    (hU.isOpenMap_subtype_val O hO) ⟨x, hxO, rfl⟩
  have hxW' : x ∈ h.restrict p U V ⁻¹' ((↑) ⁻¹' W) := hxW
  refine ⟨(↑) ⁻¹' W, hW.preimage continuous_subtype_val, hxW', ?_⟩
  intro z hz
  have hsub : (↑) '' connectedComponentIn (h.restrict p U V ⁻¹' ((↑) ⁻¹' W)) x ⊆
      connectedComponentIn (p ⁻¹' W) (x : X) := by
    refine (isPreconnected_connectedComponentIn.image _
      continuous_subtype_val.continuousOn).subset_connectedComponentIn
      ⟨x, mem_connectedComponentIn hxW', rfl⟩ ?_
    rintro _ ⟨w, hw, rfl⟩
    exact (connectedComponentIn_subset (h.restrict p U V ⁻¹' ((↑) ⁻¹' W)) x hw :)
  obtain ⟨o, ho, hoz⟩ := hWO (hsub ⟨z, hz, rfl⟩)
  rwa [← Subtype.ext hoz]


/-! ### The category of spreads -/

/-- `def:category_spreads`. An object of the category of spreads: a spread `p : X → Y`. -/
structure Spread : Type (u + 1) where
  /-- The source. -/
  X : Type u
  /-- The target. -/
  Y : Type u
  [topX : TopologicalSpace X]
  [topY : TopologicalSpace Y]
  /-- The spread map. -/
  p : X → Y
  isSpread : IsSpread p

attribute [instance] Spread.topX Spread.topY

namespace Spread

open CategoryTheory

/-- `def:category_spreads`. A morphism of spreads `(f, g)`: continuous maps `g : X → X'` and
`f : Y → Y'` with `p' ∘ g = f ∘ p`. -/
@[ext]
structure Hom (S T : Spread.{u}) where
  /-- The map of sources. -/
  g : C(S.X, T.X)
  /-- The map of targets. -/
  f : C(S.Y, T.Y)
  comm : ∀ x, T.p (g x) = f (S.p x)

instance : CategoryTheory.Category Spread.{u} where
  Hom := Hom
  id S := ⟨ContinuousMap.id _, ContinuousMap.id _, fun _ => rfl⟩
  comp φ ψ := ⟨ψ.g.comp φ.g, ψ.f.comp φ.f, fun x => by simp [ψ.comm, φ.comm]⟩

@[simp] theorem id_g (S : Spread.{u}) : (𝟙 S : Hom S S).g = ContinuousMap.id _ := rfl
@[simp] theorem id_f (S : Spread.{u}) : (𝟙 S : Hom S S).f = ContinuousMap.id _ := rfl
@[simp] theorem comp_g {S T R : Spread.{u}} (φ : S ⟶ T) (ψ : T ⟶ R) :
    Hom.g (φ ≫ ψ) = (Hom.g ψ).comp (Hom.g φ) := rfl
@[simp] theorem comp_f {S T R : Spread.{u}} (φ : S ⟶ T) (ψ : T ⟶ R) :
    Hom.f (φ ≫ ψ) = (Hom.f ψ).comp (Hom.f φ) := rfl

/-- An isomorphism of spreads gives a homeomorphism of the sources. -/
def Iso.homeoX {S T : Spread.{u}} (e : S ≅ T) : S.X ≃ₜ T.X where
  toFun := Hom.g e.hom
  invFun := Hom.g e.inv
  left_inv x := by
    have := congrArg (fun φ : S ⟶ S => Hom.g φ x) e.hom_inv_id
    exact this
  right_inv x := by
    have := congrArg (fun φ : T ⟶ T => Hom.g φ x) e.inv_hom_id
    exact this
  continuous_toFun := (Hom.g e.hom).continuous
  continuous_invFun := (Hom.g e.inv).continuous

/-- An isomorphism of spreads gives a homeomorphism of the targets. -/
def Iso.homeoY {S T : Spread.{u}} (e : S ≅ T) : S.Y ≃ₜ T.Y where
  toFun := Hom.f e.hom
  invFun := Hom.f e.inv
  left_inv x := by
    have := congrArg (fun φ : S ⟶ S => Hom.f φ x) e.hom_inv_id
    exact this
  right_inv x := by
    have := congrArg (fun φ : T ⟶ T => Hom.f φ x) e.inv_hom_id
    exact this
  continuous_toFun := (Hom.f e.hom).continuous
  continuous_invFun := (Hom.f e.inv).continuous

end Spread


/-! ### The ordinary locus -/

/-- `def:continuous_map_ordinary_locus`. A subset `U ⊆ Y` is *evenly covered* by `p` if `p` maps
each connected component of `p ⁻¹' U` homeomorphically onto `U`. -/
def IsEvenlyCoveredSet (p : X → Y) (U : Set Y) : Prop :=
  ∀ x ∈ p ⁻¹' U, ∃ e : connectedComponentIn (p ⁻¹' U) x ≃ₜ U, ∀ z, (e z : Y) = p z

/-- `def:continuous_map_ordinary_locus`. The ordinary locus `ord_p(Y)`: the points of `Y` with an
open neighbourhood evenly covered by `p`. -/
def ordY (p : X → Y) : Set Y :=
  {y | ∃ U : Set Y, IsOpen U ∧ y ∈ U ∧ IsEvenlyCoveredSet p U}

/-- `def:continuous_map_ordinary_locus`. The ordinary locus `ord_p(X) = p⁻¹(ord_p(Y))`. -/
def ordX (p : X → Y) : Set X :=
  p ⁻¹' ordY p

variable {p : X → Y}

theorem mem_ordX {x : X} : x ∈ ordX p ↔ p x ∈ ordY p := Iff.rfl

/-- With the paper's definition, a set with empty preimage is (vacuously) evenly covered. -/
theorem isEvenlyCoveredSet_of_preimage_eq_empty {U : Set Y} (h : p ⁻¹' U = ∅) :
    IsEvenlyCoveredSet p U := fun x hx => by
  rw [h] at hx; exact absurd hx (notMem_empty x)

theorem subset_ordY_of_preimage_eq_empty {U : Set Y} (hU : IsOpen U) (h : p ⁻¹' U = ∅) :
    U ⊆ ordY p := fun _ hy => ⟨U, hU, hy, isEvenlyCoveredSet_of_preimage_eq_empty h⟩

/-- Every point off the closure of the image is ordinary (vacuously). -/
theorem compl_closure_range_subset_ordY : (closure (range p))ᶜ ⊆ ordY p := by
  refine subset_ordY_of_preimage_eq_empty isClosed_closure.isOpen_compl ?_
  ext x
  simp only [mem_preimage, mem_compl_iff, mem_empty_iff_false, iff_false, not_not]
  exact subset_closure (mem_range_self x)

/-- `rem:ordinary_locii_open_but`. The ordinary locus of `Y` is open. -/
theorem isOpen_ordY : IsOpen (ordY p) := by
  rw [isOpen_iff_forall_mem_open]
  rintro y ⟨U, hU, hyU, hcov⟩
  exact ⟨U, fun y' hy' => ⟨U, hU, hy', hcov⟩, hU, hyU⟩

/-- `rem:ordinary_locii_open_but`. The ordinary locus of `X` is open. -/
theorem isOpen_ordX (hp : Continuous p) : IsOpen (ordX p) :=
  isOpen_ordY.preimage hp

theorem IsEvenlyCoveredSet.injOn {U : Set Y} (hU : IsEvenlyCoveredSet p U) {x : X}
    (hx : x ∈ p ⁻¹' U) : InjOn p (connectedComponentIn (p ⁻¹' U) x) := by
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := hU x hx
  intro a ha b hb hab
  have : e ⟨a, ha⟩ = e ⟨b, hb⟩ := Subtype.ext (by rw [he, he]; exact hab)
  exact congrArg Subtype.val (e.injective this)

theorem IsEvenlyCoveredSet.image_eq {U : Set Y} (hU : IsEvenlyCoveredSet p U) {x : X}
    (hx : x ∈ p ⁻¹' U) : p '' connectedComponentIn (p ⁻¹' U) x = U := by
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := hU x hx
  ext y
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨z, hz, rfl⟩; exact (connectedComponentIn_subset (p ⁻¹' U) x hz :)
  · intro hy
    refine ⟨e.symm ⟨y, hy⟩, (e.symm ⟨y, hy⟩).2, ?_⟩
    rw [← he, e.apply_symm_apply]

/-- A preconnected set covered by pairwise disjoint open sets lies in the one it meets. -/
theorem IsPreconnected.subset_of_pairwiseDisjoint {ι : Type*} {s : Set X} (hs : IsPreconnected s)
    {S : ι → Set X} (hSo : ∀ i, IsOpen (S i)) (hd : Pairwise (Disjoint on S))
    (hsub : s ⊆ ⋃ i, S i) {i : ι} {a : X} (has : a ∈ s) (hai : a ∈ S i) : s ⊆ S i := by
  classical
  refine hs.subset_left_of_subset_union (v := ⋃ j, ⋃ (_ : j ≠ i), S j) (hSo i)
    (isOpen_iUnion fun j => isOpen_iUnion fun _ => hSo j) ?_ ?_ ⟨a, has, hai⟩
  · rw [disjoint_iUnion_right]; intro j; rw [disjoint_iUnion_right]; intro hj
    exact hd (Ne.symm hj)
  · intro z hz
    obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ := mem_iUnion.1 (hsub hz)
    by_cases hji : j = i
    · subst hji; exact Or.inl hj
    · exact Or.inr (mem_iUnion.2 ⟨j, mem_iUnion.2 ⟨hji, hj⟩⟩)

/-- Sheets give an evenly covered set: if `p⁻¹(U)` is the disjoint union of open preconnected
sets each mapped homeomorphically onto `U`, then `U` is evenly covered. -/
theorem isEvenlyCoveredSet_of_sheets {ι : Type*} {U : Set Y} (S : ι → Set X)
    (hSo : ∀ i, IsOpen (S i)) (hSc : ∀ i, IsPreconnected (S i)) (hd : Pairwise (Disjoint on S))
    (hcov : p ⁻¹' U = ⋃ i, S i) (hhom : ∀ i, ∃ e : S i ≃ₜ U, ∀ z, (e z : Y) = p z) :
    IsEvenlyCoveredSet p U := by
  intro x hx
  obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := mem_iUnion.1 (hcov ▸ hx : x ∈ ⋃ i, S i)
  have hC : connectedComponentIn (p ⁻¹' U) x = S i := by
    apply subset_antisymm
    · exact IsPreconnected.subset_of_pairwiseDisjoint isPreconnected_connectedComponentIn hSo hd
        (hcov ▸ connectedComponentIn_subset _ _) (mem_connectedComponentIn hx) hi
    · exact (hSc i).subset_connectedComponentIn hi (hcov ▸ subset_iUnion S i)
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := hhom i
  exact ⟨(Homeomorph.setCongr hC).trans e, fun z => he _⟩

/-- An ordinary point of `X` has a neighbourhood on which `p` is injective (when `X` is locally
connected): the component of an evenly covered open set. -/
theorem exists_injOn_of_mem_ordX [LocallyConnectedSpace X] (hp : Continuous p) {x : X}
    (hx : x ∈ ordX p) : ∃ V, IsOpen V ∧ x ∈ V ∧ InjOn p V := by
  obtain ⟨U, hU, hxU, hcov⟩ := hx
  exact ⟨_, (hU.preimage hp).connectedComponentIn, mem_connectedComponentIn hxU,
    hcov.injOn hxU⟩

theorem notMem_ordY_of_forall_not_injOn [LocallyConnectedSpace X] (hp : Continuous p) {x : X}
    (h : ∀ V, IsOpen V → x ∈ V → ¬ InjOn p V) : p x ∉ ordY p := fun hx => by
  obtain ⟨V, hV, hxV, hinj⟩ := exists_injOn_of_mem_ordX hp hx
  exact h V hV hxV hinj

/-- `rem:singular_on_singular`. For a surjective map, `p(X ∖ ord(X)) = Y ∖ ord(Y)`.
(The paper also asks `p` continuous; this is not used.) -/
theorem image_compl_ordX (hp : Function.Surjective p) : p '' (ordX p)ᶜ = (ordY p)ᶜ := by
  rw [ordX, ← preimage_compl, image_preimage_eq _ hp]


/-- An evenly covered open set (paper's sense) over a locally connected source gives an evenly
covered point in mathlib's sense. -/
theorem isEvenlyCovered_of_isEvenlyCoveredSet [LocallyConnectedSpace X] (hp : Continuous p)
    {U : Set Y} (hU : IsOpen U) (hcov : IsEvenlyCoveredSet p U) {y : Y} (hy : y ∈ U) :
    IsEvenlyCovered p y (p ⁻¹' {y}) := by
  rcases (p ⁻¹' U).eq_empty_or_nonempty with h | ⟨x₀, hx₀⟩
  · haveI : IsEmpty (p ⁻¹' {y}) := by
      rw [isEmpty_subtype]
      intro x hx
      have hxU : x ∈ p ⁻¹' U := by
        rw [mem_preimage, (hx : p x = y)]; exact hy
      rw [h] at hxU; exact hxU
    exact IsEvenlyCovered.of_preimage_eq_empty _ (hU.mem_nhds hy) h
  · let ι := {C : Set X // ∃ x ∈ p ⁻¹' U, C = connectedComponentIn (p ⁻¹' U) x}
    letI : TopologicalSpace ι := ⊥
    haveI : DiscreteTopology ι := ⟨rfl⟩
    haveI : Nonempty ι := ⟨⟨_, x₀, hx₀, rfl⟩⟩
    haveI : Nonempty (Y → X) := ⟨fun _ => x₀⟩
    have hopenC : ∀ i : ι, IsOpen i.1 := by
      rintro ⟨_, x, hx, rfl⟩; exact (hU.preimage hp).connectedComponentIn
    have open_iff : ∀ (i : ι) {W : Set Y}, W ⊆ U → (IsOpen W ↔ IsOpen (p ⁻¹' W ∩ i.1)) := by
      rintro ⟨C, x, hx, rfl⟩ W hWU
      refine ⟨fun hW => (hW.preimage hp).inter (hopenC ⟨_, x, hx, rfl⟩), fun h => ?_⟩
      obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := hcov x hx
      set O : Set (connectedComponentIn (p ⁻¹' U) x) := {c | p c ∈ W} with hOdef
      have hO : IsOpen O := by
        have : O = (↑) ⁻¹' (p ⁻¹' W ∩ connectedComponentIn (p ⁻¹' U) x) := by
          ext c; simp [O]
        rw [this]; exact h.preimage continuous_subtype_val
      have hW : W = (↑) '' (e '' O) := by
        ext w
        constructor
        · intro hw
          refine ⟨⟨w, hWU hw⟩, ⟨e.symm ⟨w, hWU hw⟩, ?_, e.apply_symm_apply _⟩, rfl⟩
          show p (e.symm ⟨w, hWU hw⟩ : X) ∈ W
          rw [← he, e.apply_symm_apply]; exact hw
        · rintro ⟨_, ⟨c, hc, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
          rw [he]; exact hc
      rw [hW]
      exact hU.isOpenMap_subtype_val _ (e.isOpenMap O hO)
    have inj : ∀ i : ι, InjOn p i.1 := by
      rintro ⟨C, x, hx, rfl⟩; exact hcov.injOn hx
    have surj : ∀ i : ι, SurjOn p i.1 U := by
      rintro ⟨C, x, hx, rfl⟩; exact (hcov.image_eq hx).ge
    have disj : Pairwise (Disjoint on fun i : ι => i.1) := by
      rintro ⟨_, x, hx, rfl⟩ ⟨_, x', hx', rfl⟩ hne
      rw [onFun, Set.disjoint_left]
      intro z hz hz'
      apply hne
      exact Subtype.ext ((connectedComponentIn_eq hz).trans (connectedComponentIn_eq hz').symm)
    have exh : p ⁻¹' U ⊆ ⋃ i : ι, i.1 := fun x hx =>
      mem_iUnion.2 ⟨⟨_, x, hx, rfl⟩, mem_connectedComponentIn hx⟩
    have hyt : y ∈ (IsOpen.trivializationDiscrete (fun i : ι => i.1) U hU open_iff inj surj disj
        exh).baseSet := by
      rw [IsOpen.trivializationDiscrete_baseSet]; exact hy
    exact (IsEvenlyCovered.of_trivialization hyt).to_isEvenlyCovered_preimage

/-- `rem:ordinary_locii_open_but`. Over a locally connected source, `p` is a covering map (in
mathlib's sense: discrete fibres, evenly covered neighbourhoods, fibres possibly empty) over its
ordinary locus. -/
theorem isCoveringMapOn_ordY [LocallyConnectedSpace X] (hp : Continuous p) :
    IsCoveringMapOn p (ordY p) := by
  rintro y ⟨U, hU, hyU, hcov⟩
  exact isEvenlyCovered_of_isEvenlyCoveredSet hp hU hcov hyU

/-- `rem:ordinary_locii_open_but`. The restriction `ord(X) → ord(Y)` is a covering map. -/
theorem isCoveringMap_restrict_ordX [LocallyConnectedSpace X] (hp : Continuous p) :
    IsCoveringMap ((ordY p).restrictPreimage p) :=
  (isCoveringMapOn_ordY hp).isCoveringMap_restrictPreimage

/-- For a surjective `p`, the restriction `ord(X) → ord(Y)` is surjective. -/
theorem surjective_restrict_ordX (hp : Function.Surjective p) :
    Function.Surjective ((ordY p).restrictPreimage p) := by
  rintro ⟨y, hy⟩
  obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := hp y
  exact ⟨⟨x, hy⟩, rfl⟩


/-! ### The partial-covering lemma -/

/-- A sheet gives a homeomorphism onto its image. -/
theorem exists_homeomorph_of_sheet (hp : Continuous p) {S : Set X} {U : Set Y} (hS : IsOpen S)
    (hinj : InjOn p S) (himg : p '' S = U) (hopen : ∀ W ⊆ S, IsOpen W → IsOpen (p '' W)) :
    ∃ e : S ≃ₜ U, ∀ z, (e z : Y) = p z := by
  let f : S → U := fun z => ⟨p z, himg ▸ mem_image_of_mem p z.2⟩
  have hf : Bijective f := by
    refine ⟨fun a b h => Subtype.ext (hinj a.2 b.2 (congrArg Subtype.val h)), fun y => ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨z, hz, hzy⟩ := (himg.symm ▸ y.2 : (y : Y) ∈ p '' S)
    exact ⟨⟨z, hz⟩, Subtype.ext hzy⟩
  have hfc : Continuous f := (hp.comp continuous_subtype_val).subtype_mk _
  have hfo : IsOpenMap f := by
    intro O hO
    have : f '' O = (↑) ⁻¹' (p '' ((↑) '' O)) := by
      ext y
      simp only [mem_image, mem_preimage, f, Subtype.ext_iff]
      constructor
      · rintro ⟨z, hz, hzy⟩; exact ⟨z, ⟨z, hz, rfl⟩, hzy⟩
      · rintro ⟨_, ⟨z, hz, rfl⟩, hzy⟩; exact ⟨z, hz, hzy⟩
    rw [this]
    exact (hopen _ (Subtype.coe_image_subset _ _) (hS.isOpenMap_subtype_val O hO)).preimage
      continuous_subtype_val
  exact ⟨(Equiv.ofBijective f hf).toHomeomorphOfContinuousOpen hfc hfo, fun z => rfl⟩

/-- The heart of `lem:spread_partial_covering`: if `p⁻¹(U) ∩ X₁` is covered by disjoint open
sheets inside the portly `X₁`, each mapped injectively and openly onto (a superset of) `U`, then
`p⁻¹(U) ⊆ X₁`. -/
theorem preimage_subset_of_sheets [T2Space X] [LocallyConnectedSpace X] (hp : Continuous p)
    {X₁ : Set X} (hX₁ : IsPortly X₁) {U : Set Y} (hU : IsOpen U) {ι : Type*} (S : ι → Set X)
    (hSo : ∀ i, IsOpen (S i)) (hd : Pairwise (Disjoint on S))
    (hcov : p ⁻¹' U ∩ X₁ ⊆ ⋃ i, S i) (hS₁ : ∀ i, S i ⊆ X₁)
    (hinj : ∀ i, InjOn p (S i)) (hsurj : ∀ i, U ⊆ p '' S i)
    (hopen : ∀ i, ∀ W ⊆ S i, IsOpen W → IsOpen (p '' W)) : p ⁻¹' U ⊆ X₁ := by
  intro x hx
  by_contra hxX₁
  set V := connectedComponentIn (p ⁻¹' U) x
  have hVo : IsOpen V := (hU.preimage hp).connectedComponentIn
  have hxV : x ∈ V := mem_connectedComponentIn hx
  have hVU : V ⊆ p ⁻¹' U := connectedComponentIn_subset _ _
  have hVc : IsPreconnected (V ∩ X₁) :=
    hX₁.locallyConnectedIn V hVo isPreconnected_connectedComponentIn
  obtain ⟨a, haV, haX₁⟩ := hX₁.dense.inter_open_nonempty V hVo ⟨x, hxV⟩
  obtain ⟨i, hai⟩ := mem_iUnion.1 (hcov ⟨hVU haV, haX₁⟩)
  have hVi : V ∩ X₁ ⊆ S i := IsPreconnected.subset_of_pairwiseDisjoint hVc hSo hd
    (fun z hz => hcov ⟨hVU hz.1, hz.2⟩) ⟨haV, haX₁⟩ hai
  have hxcl : x ∈ closure (S i) := closure_mono hVi (hX₁.dense.open_subset_closure_inter hVo hxV)
  obtain ⟨x', hx'i, hx'x⟩ := hsurj i hx
  have hne : x ≠ x' := fun h => hxX₁ (h ▸ hS₁ i hx'i)
  obtain ⟨W, W', hW, hW', hxW, hx'W', hWW'⟩ := t2_separation hne
  have hW'' : IsOpen (p '' (W' ∩ S i)) := hopen i _ inter_subset_right (hW'.inter (hSo i))
  have hpx : p x ∈ p '' (W' ∩ S i) := ⟨x', ⟨hx'W', hx'i⟩, hx'x⟩
  have hN : IsOpen (W ∩ p ⁻¹' (p '' (W' ∩ S i))) := hW.inter (hW''.preimage hp)
  obtain ⟨z, ⟨hzW, hzp⟩, hzi⟩ := mem_closure_iff.1 hxcl _ hN ⟨hxW, hpx⟩
  obtain ⟨w, ⟨hwW', hwi⟩, hwz⟩ := hzp
  have hwz' : w = z := hinj i hwi hzi hwz
  exact Set.disjoint_left.1 hWW' hzW (hwz' ▸ hwW')

/-- `lem:spread_partial_covering`. Let `p : X → Y` be continuous, inducing a covering map
`X₁ → Y₁` with `X₁` portly and `Y₁` open. Then `Y₁ ⊆ ord(Y)`, `X₁ ⊆ ord(X)` and
`p⁻¹(Y₁) = X₁`. -/
theorem spread_partial_covering [T2Space X] [LocallyConnectedSpace X]
    (hp : Continuous p) {X₁ : Set X} {Y₁ : Set Y} (hX₁ : IsPortly X₁) (hY₁ : IsOpen Y₁)
    (hmaps : MapsTo p X₁ Y₁) (hcov : IsCoveringMap (hmaps.restrict p X₁ Y₁)) :
    Y₁ ⊆ ordY p ∧ X₁ ⊆ ordX p ∧ p ⁻¹' Y₁ = X₁ := by
  have key : ∀ y ∈ Y₁, ∃ U, IsOpen U ∧ y ∈ U ∧ IsEvenlyCoveredSet p U ∧ p ⁻¹' U ⊆ X₁ := by
    intro y hy
    set r := hmaps.restrict p X₁ Y₁ with hr
    set I := r ⁻¹' {(⟨y, hy⟩ : Y₁)} with hI
    obtain ⟨hdisc, U', hyU', hU', hrU', H, hH⟩ := hcov ⟨y, hy⟩
    have hrp : ∀ z : X₁, (r z : Y) = p z := fun _ => rfl
    -- the sheets over `U'`, seen in `X`
    let S₀ : I → Set X := fun i =>
      (↑) '' ((↑) '' ((fun z : r ⁻¹' U' => (H z).2) ⁻¹' {i}) : Set X₁)
    have mem_S₀ : ∀ i x, x ∈ S₀ i ↔ ∃ z : r ⁻¹' U', ((z : X₁) : X) = x ∧ (H z).2 = i := by
      intro i x
      constructor
      · rintro ⟨_, ⟨z, hz, rfl⟩, rfl⟩; exact ⟨z, rfl, hz⟩
      · rintro ⟨z, rfl, hz⟩; exact ⟨_, ⟨z, hz, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
    have hU'o : IsOpen ((↑) '' U' : Set Y) := hY₁.isOpenMap_subtype_val _ hU'
    have hyU'' : y ∈ ((↑) '' U' : Set Y) := ⟨_, hyU', rfl⟩
    have hS₀o : ∀ i, IsOpen (S₀ i) := fun i =>
      hX₁.isOpen.isOpenMap_subtype_val _ (hrU'.isOpenMap_subtype_val _
        ((isOpen_discrete {i}).preimage (continuous_snd.comp H.continuous)))
    have hS₀₁ : ∀ i, S₀ i ⊆ X₁ := fun i => Subtype.coe_image_subset _ _
    have hS₀inj : ∀ i, InjOn p (S₀ i) := by
      intro i x₁ hx₁ x₂ hx₂ h12
      obtain ⟨z₁, rfl, hz₁⟩ := (mem_S₀ i x₁).1 hx₁
      obtain ⟨z₂, rfl, hz₂⟩ := (mem_S₀ i x₂).1 hx₂
      have h1 : (H z₁).1 = (H z₂).1 := Subtype.ext (by
        rw [hH, hH]; exact Subtype.ext h12)
      have : z₁ = z₂ := H.injective (Prod.ext h1 (hz₁.trans hz₂.symm))
      rw [this]
    have hS₀surj : ∀ i, (↑) '' U' ⊆ p '' S₀ i := by
      rintro i _ ⟨u, hu, rfl⟩
      refine ⟨((H.symm (⟨u, hu⟩, i) : X₁) : X), (mem_S₀ i _).2 ⟨_, rfl, ?_⟩, ?_⟩
      · rw [H.apply_symm_apply]
      · rw [← hrp, ← hH, H.apply_symm_apply]
    have hS₀cov : p ⁻¹' ((↑) '' U') ∩ X₁ ⊆ ⋃ i, S₀ i := by
      rintro x ⟨⟨u, hu, hux⟩, hxX₁⟩
      have hrx : r ⟨x, hxX₁⟩ ∈ U' := by
        have : r ⟨x, hxX₁⟩ = u := Subtype.ext hux.symm
        rw [this]; exact hu
      exact mem_iUnion.2 ⟨(H ⟨⟨x, hxX₁⟩, hrx⟩).2, (mem_S₀ _ x).2 ⟨⟨⟨x, hxX₁⟩, hrx⟩, rfl, rfl⟩⟩
    have hS₀d : Pairwise (Disjoint on S₀) := by
      intro i j hij
      rw [onFun, Set.disjoint_left]
      intro x hxi hxj
      obtain ⟨z₁, rfl, hz₁⟩ := (mem_S₀ i x).1 hxi
      obtain ⟨z₂, hz₁₂, hz₂⟩ := (mem_S₀ j _).1 hxj
      have : z₂ = z₁ := Subtype.ext (Subtype.ext hz₁₂)
      exact hij (hz₁.symm.trans (this ▸ hz₂))
    have hS₀open : ∀ i, ∀ W ⊆ S₀ i, IsOpen W → IsOpen (p '' W) := by
      intro i W hWS hW
      have hWX₁ : W ⊆ X₁ := hWS.trans (hS₀₁ i)
      have : p '' W = (↑) '' (r '' ((↑) ⁻¹' W)) := by
        ext y'
        constructor
        · rintro ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩; exact ⟨_, ⟨⟨x, hWX₁ hx⟩, hx, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
        · rintro ⟨_, ⟨z, hz, rfl⟩, rfl⟩; exact ⟨z, hz, rfl⟩
      rw [this]
      exact hY₁.isOpenMap_subtype_val _ (hcov.isOpenMap _ (hW.preimage continuous_subtype_val))
    -- no sheet: the preimage of `U'` is empty
    rcases isEmpty_or_nonempty I with hIe | ⟨⟨i₀⟩⟩
    · have hsub := preimage_subset_of_sheets hp hX₁ hU'o S₀ hS₀o hS₀d hS₀cov hS₀₁ hS₀inj
        hS₀surj hS₀open
      have hempty : p ⁻¹' ((↑) '' U') = ∅ := eq_empty_of_forall_notMem fun x hx => by
        obtain ⟨i, -⟩ := mem_iUnion.1 (hS₀cov ⟨hx, hsub hx⟩)
        exact hIe.elim i
      exact ⟨_, hU'o, hyU'', isEvenlyCoveredSet_of_preimage_eq_empty hempty,
        by rw [hempty]; exact empty_subset _⟩
    -- a sheet makes `U'` locally connected near `y`; shrink to the connected `U`
    have hS₀img : p '' S₀ i₀ = (↑) '' U' := by
      refine subset_antisymm ?_ (hS₀surj i₀)
      rintro _ ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
      obtain ⟨z, rfl, -⟩ := (mem_S₀ i₀ x).1 hx
      exact ⟨r z, z.2, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨e₀, -⟩ := exists_homeomorph_of_sheet hp (hS₀o i₀) (hS₀inj i₀) hS₀img (hS₀open i₀)
    haveI : LocallyConnectedSpace (S₀ i₀) := (hS₀o i₀).locallyConnectedSpace
    haveI : LocallyConnectedSpace ((↑) '' U' : Set Y) := e₀.symm.isOpenEmbedding.locallyConnectedSpace
    set U := connectedComponentIn ((↑) '' U' : Set Y) y
    have hUo : IsOpen U := by
      rw [show U = _ from connectedComponentIn_eq_image hyU'']
      exact hU'o.isOpenMap_subtype_val _ isOpen_connectedComponent
    have hyU : y ∈ U := mem_connectedComponentIn hyU''
    have hUU' : U ⊆ (↑) '' U' := connectedComponentIn_subset _ _
    have hUc : IsPreconnected U := isPreconnected_connectedComponentIn
    let S : I → Set X := fun i => S₀ i ∩ p ⁻¹' U
    have hSo : ∀ i, IsOpen (S i) := fun i => (hS₀o i).inter (hUo.preimage hp)
    have hSd : Pairwise (Disjoint on S) := fun i j hij =>
      (hS₀d hij).mono inter_subset_left inter_subset_left
    have hScov : p ⁻¹' U ∩ X₁ ⊆ ⋃ i, S i := by
      intro x hx
      obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := mem_iUnion.1 (hS₀cov ⟨hUU' hx.1, hx.2⟩)
      exact mem_iUnion.2 ⟨i, hi, hx.1⟩
    have hSsurj : ∀ i, U ⊆ p '' S i := by
      intro i y' hy'
      obtain ⟨x, hx, hxy⟩ := hS₀surj i (hUU' hy')
      exact ⟨x, ⟨hx, by rw [mem_preimage, hxy]; exact hy'⟩, hxy⟩
    have hsub : p ⁻¹' U ⊆ X₁ := preimage_subset_of_sheets hp hX₁ hUo S hSo hSd hScov
      (fun i => inter_subset_left.trans (hS₀₁ i)) (fun i => (hS₀inj i).mono inter_subset_left)
      hSsurj (fun i W hW => hS₀open i W (hW.trans inter_subset_left))
    refine ⟨U, hUo, hyU, ?_, hsub⟩
    have hhom : ∀ i, ∃ e : S i ≃ₜ U, ∀ z, (e z : Y) = p z := fun i =>
      exists_homeomorph_of_sheet hp (hSo i) ((hS₀inj i).mono inter_subset_left)
        (subset_antisymm (by rintro _ ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩; exact hx.2) (hSsurj i))
        (fun W hW => hS₀open i W (hW.trans inter_subset_left))
    refine isEvenlyCoveredSet_of_sheets S hSo (fun i => ?_) hSd ?_ hhom
    · obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := hhom i
      have : S i = range (fun u : U => (e.symm u : X)) := by
        ext x
        constructor
        · intro hx; exact ⟨e ⟨x, hx⟩, by simp⟩
        · rintro ⟨u, rfl⟩; exact (e.symm u).2
      rw [this]
      haveI := isPreconnected_iff_preconnectedSpace.1 hUc
      exact isPreconnected_range (continuous_subtype_val.comp e.symm.continuous)
    · apply subset_antisymm
      · intro x hx; exact hScov ⟨hx, hsub hx⟩
      · intro x hx
        obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := mem_iUnion.1 hx
        exact hi.2
  have hpre : p ⁻¹' Y₁ = X₁ := by
    apply subset_antisymm
    · intro x hx
      obtain ⟨U, -, hxU, -, hsub⟩ := key (p x) hx
      exact hsub hxU
    · exact hmaps
  have hY : Y₁ ⊆ ordY p := fun y hy => by
    obtain ⟨U, hU, hyU, hcovU, -⟩ := key y hy
    exact ⟨U, hU, hyU, hcovU⟩
  refine ⟨hY, fun x hx => hY (hmaps hx), hpre⟩


/-! ### Invariance of the ordinary locus under isomorphisms -/

section Iso

variable {X' Y' : Type*} [TopologicalSpace X'] [TopologicalSpace Y'] {p' : X' → Y'}

/-- Homeomorphisms `g`, `f` with `p' ∘ g = f ∘ p` carry evenly covered sets to evenly covered
sets. -/
theorem IsEvenlyCoveredSet.image_homeomorph (g : X ≃ₜ X') (f : Y ≃ₜ Y')
    (hcomm : ∀ x, p' (g x) = f (p x)) {U : Set Y} (hU : IsEvenlyCoveredSet p U) :
    IsEvenlyCoveredSet p' (f '' U) := by
  have hpre : p' ⁻¹' (f '' U) = g '' (p ⁻¹' U) := by
    ext x'
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨u, hu, hux⟩
      refine ⟨g.symm x', ?_, g.apply_symm_apply x'⟩
      show p (g.symm x') ∈ U
      have : f (p (g.symm x')) = f u := by rw [← hcomm, g.apply_symm_apply, hux]
      rwa [f.injective this]
    · rintro ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
      exact ⟨p x, hx, (hcomm x).symm⟩
  intro x' hx'
  have hx'' := hx'
  rw [hpre] at hx''
  obtain ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩ := hx''
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := hU x hx
  have hC : connectedComponentIn (p' ⁻¹' (f '' U)) (g x) =
      g '' connectedComponentIn (p ⁻¹' U) x := by
    rw [hpre, g.image_connectedComponentIn hx]
  refine ⟨(Homeomorph.setCongr hC).trans ((g.image _).symm.trans (e.trans (f.image U))),
    fun z => ?_⟩
  set c := (g.image (connectedComponentIn (p ⁻¹' U) x)).symm (Homeomorph.setCongr hC z) with hc
  have hcz : g (c : X) = z := by
    have := (g.image (connectedComponentIn (p ⁻¹' U) x)).apply_symm_apply
      (Homeomorph.setCongr hC z)
    exact congrArg Subtype.val this
  have : ((((Homeomorph.setCongr hC).trans ((g.image _).symm.trans (e.trans (f.image U)))) z :
      f '' U) : Y') = f (e c) := rfl
  rw [this, he, ← hcomm, hcz]

/-- `lem:ord_iso`, on the target: `f(ord(Y₁)) = ord(Y₂)`. Only the homeomorphisms and the
commutation are used. -/
theorem image_ordY_of_homeomorph (g : X ≃ₜ X') (f : Y ≃ₜ Y')
    (hcomm : ∀ x, p' (g x) = f (p x)) : f '' ordY p = ordY p' := by
  have hcomm' : ∀ x', p (g.symm x') = f.symm (p' x') := fun x' => by
    rw [eq_comm, f.symm_apply_eq, ← hcomm, g.apply_symm_apply]
  apply subset_antisymm
  · rintro _ ⟨y, ⟨U, hU, hyU, hcov⟩, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨f '' U, f.isOpenMap U hU, mem_image_of_mem f hyU, hcov.image_homeomorph g f hcomm⟩
  · rintro y' ⟨U, hU, hyU, hcov⟩
    refine ⟨f.symm y', ⟨f.symm '' U, f.symm.isOpenMap U hU, mem_image_of_mem _ hyU,
      hcov.image_homeomorph g.symm f.symm hcomm'⟩, f.apply_symm_apply y'⟩

/-- `lem:ord_iso`, on the source: `g(ord(X₁)) = ord(X₂)`. -/
theorem image_ordX_of_homeomorph (g : X ≃ₜ X') (f : Y ≃ₜ Y')
    (hcomm : ∀ x, p' (g x) = f (p x)) : g '' ordX p = ordX p' := by
  ext x'
  rw [← g.apply_symm_apply x', g.image_eq_preimage_symm, mem_preimage, g.symm_apply_apply,
    mem_ordX, mem_ordX, hcomm, ← image_ordY_of_homeomorph g f hcomm]
  exact (f.injective.mem_set_image).symm

end Iso

/-- `lem:ord_iso`. A spread isomorphism `(f, g)` satisfies `g(ord(X₁)) = ord(X₂)` and
`f(ord(Y₁)) = ord(Y₂)`. -/
theorem Spread.ord_iso {S T : Spread.{u}} (e : S ≅ T) :
    Spread.Hom.g e.hom '' ordX S.p = ordX T.p ∧ Spread.Hom.f e.hom '' ordY S.p = ordY T.p :=
  ⟨image_ordX_of_homeomorph (Spread.Iso.homeoX e) (Spread.Iso.homeoY e) (Spread.Hom.comm e.hom),
    image_ordY_of_homeomorph (Spread.Iso.homeoX e) (Spread.Iso.homeoY e) (Spread.Hom.comm e.hom)⟩


/-! ### `cex:portlyness`, first item: without openness of `X₁` -/

/-- `cex:portlyness`, first item. If `p` maps `X₁` into an open `Y₁` by an open map (e.g. a
covering map) and `x ∈ X₁` is not interior to `X₁`, then `p` is injective on no open
neighbourhood of `x`. -/
theorem not_injOn_of_notMem_interior (hp : Continuous p) {X₁ : Set X} {Y₁ : Set Y}
    (hY₁ : IsOpen Y₁) (hmaps : MapsTo p X₁ Y₁) (hopen : IsOpenMap (hmaps.restrict p X₁ Y₁))
    {x : X} (hx : x ∈ X₁) (hxi : x ∉ interior X₁) {V : Set X} (hV : IsOpen V) (hxV : x ∈ V) :
    ¬ InjOn p V := by
  intro hinj
  set N : Set X₁ := (↑) ⁻¹' V
  have hN : IsOpen N := hV.preimage continuous_subtype_val
  have hpN : IsOpen ((↑) '' (hmaps.restrict p X₁ Y₁ '' N) : Set Y) :=
    hY₁.isOpenMap_subtype_val _ (hopen N hN)
  set V'' := V ∩ p ⁻¹' ((↑) '' (hmaps.restrict p X₁ Y₁ '' N))
  have hV''o : IsOpen V'' := hV.inter (hpN.preimage hp)
  have hxV'' : x ∈ V'' := ⟨hxV, _, ⟨⟨x, hx⟩, hxV, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
  have hnot : ¬ V'' ⊆ X₁ := fun h => hxi (mem_interior.2 ⟨V'', h, hV''o, hxV''⟩)
  obtain ⟨z, hzV'', hzX₁⟩ := not_subset.1 hnot
  obtain ⟨_, ⟨n, hn, rfl⟩, hnz⟩ := hzV''.2
  have hnz' : (n : X) = z := hinj hn hzV''.1 hnz
  exact hzX₁ (hnz' ▸ n.2)

/-- `cex:portlyness`, first item: a non-interior point of `X₁` is singular, so the conclusion
`X₁ ⊆ ord(X)` of `lem:spread_partial_covering` fails when `X₁` is not open. -/
theorem notMem_ordX_of_notMem_interior [LocallyConnectedSpace X] (hp : Continuous p)
    {X₁ : Set X} {Y₁ : Set Y} (hY₁ : IsOpen Y₁) (hmaps : MapsTo p X₁ Y₁)
    (hcov : IsCoveringMap (hmaps.restrict p X₁ Y₁)) {x : X} (hx : x ∈ X₁)
    (hxi : x ∉ interior X₁) : x ∉ ordX p ∧ p x ∉ ordY p := by
  have h : p x ∉ ordY p := notMem_ordY_of_forall_not_injOn hp fun V hV hxV =>
    not_injOn_of_notMem_interior hp hY₁ hmaps hcov.isOpenMap hx hxi hV hxV
  exact ⟨h, h⟩

/-! ### Homeomorphisms are covering maps -/

theorem isCoveringMap_of_homeomorph {E B : Type*} [TopologicalSpace E] [TopologicalSpace B]
    [T2Space E] (e : E ≃ₜ B) : IsCoveringMap e := by
  rw [isCoveringMap_iff_isCoveringMapOn_univ]
  refine e.isClosedMap.isCoveringMapOn_of_openPartialHomeomorph (fun y _ => ?_) ?_
  · refine Set.Subsingleton.finite ?_
    intro a ha b hb
    exact e.injective (ha.trans hb.symm)
  · intro x _
    exact ⟨e.toOpenPartialHomeomorph, mem_univ x, rfl⟩


/-! ### Spreads on the real line: locally distance-preserving maps -/

/-- A self-map of `ℝ` that locally preserves the distance to each point (slopes `± 1`). -/
def IsLocDistPres (f : ℝ → ℝ) : Prop :=
  ∀ x, ∃ r > 0, ∀ z, |z - x| < r → |f z - f x| = |z - x|

theorem IsLocDistPres.comp {f g : ℝ → ℝ} (hg : IsLocDistPres g) (hf : IsLocDistPres f) :
    IsLocDistPres (g ∘ f) := by
  intro x
  obtain ⟨r₁, hr₁, h₁⟩ := hf x
  obtain ⟨r₂, hr₂, h₂⟩ := hg (f x)
  refine ⟨min r₁ r₂, lt_min hr₁ hr₂, fun z hz => ?_⟩
  have hz₁ := h₁ z (hz.trans_le (min_le_left _ _))
  have hz₂ := h₂ (f z) (by rw [hz₁]; exact hz.trans_le (min_le_right _ _))
  simp only [comp_apply]; rw [hz₂, hz₁]

theorem isLocDistPres_abs : IsLocDistPres (fun x : ℝ => |x|) := by
  intro x
  rcases lt_trichotomy x 0 with hx | rfl | hx
  · refine ⟨-x, neg_pos.2 hx, fun z hz => ?_⟩
    have hz0 : z < 0 := by
      have := (abs_lt.1 hz).2; linarith
    show abs (|z| - |x|) = |z - x|
    rw [abs_of_neg hz0, abs_of_neg hx, show -z - -x = -(z - x) by ring, abs_neg]
  · exact ⟨1, one_pos, fun z _ => by simp⟩
  · refine ⟨x, hx, fun z hz => ?_⟩
    have hz0 : 0 < z := by
      have := (abs_lt.1 hz).1; linarith
    show abs (|z| - |x|) = |z - x|
    rw [abs_of_pos hz0, abs_of_pos hx]

theorem isLocDistPres_sub_const (c : ℝ) : IsLocDistPres (fun x : ℝ => x - c) :=
  fun _ => ⟨1, one_pos, fun z _ => by ring_nf⟩

theorem IsLocDistPres.continuous {f : ℝ → ℝ} (hf : IsLocDistPres f) : Continuous f := by
  rw [Metric.continuous_iff]
  intro b ε hε
  obtain ⟨r, hr, h⟩ := hf b
  refine ⟨min r ε, lt_min hr hε, fun a ha => ?_⟩
  rw [Real.dist_eq] at ha ⊢
  rw [h a (ha.trans_le (min_le_left _ _))]
  exact ha.trans_le (min_le_right _ _)

/-- A locally distance-preserving self-map of `ℝ` is a spread. -/
theorem IsLocDistPres.isSpread {f : ℝ → ℝ} (hf : IsLocDistPres f) : IsSpread f := by
  refine isSpread_iff_of_locallyConnectedSpace.2 ⟨hf.continuous, fun x O hO hxO => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨ε, hε, hεO⟩ := Metric.isOpen_iff.1 hO x hxO
  obtain ⟨r, hr, h⟩ := hf x
  set δ := min ε r / 2 with hδ
  have hδpos : 0 < δ := by positivity
  have hδε : δ < ε := by have := min_le_left ε r; linarith
  have hδr : δ < r := by have := min_le_right ε r; linarith
  refine ⟨Metric.ball (f x) δ, Metric.isOpen_ball, Metric.mem_ball_self hδpos, ?_⟩
  intro z hz
  have hxC : x ∈ connectedComponentIn (f ⁻¹' Metric.ball (f x) δ) x :=
    mem_connectedComponentIn (Metric.mem_ball_self hδpos)
  have hord := isPreconnected_iff_ordConnected.1
    (isPreconnected_connectedComponentIn (x := x) (F := f ⁻¹' Metric.ball (f x) δ))
  apply hεO
  rw [Metric.mem_ball, Real.dist_eq]
  suffices hzδ : |z - x| < δ by linarith
  by_contra hzx'
  have hzx : δ ≤ |z - x| := not_lt.1 hzx'
  have key : ∀ w, w ∈ connectedComponentIn (f ⁻¹' Metric.ball (f x) δ) x → |w - x| = δ → False := by
    intro w hw hwx
    have := connectedComponentIn_subset _ _ hw
    rw [mem_preimage, Metric.mem_ball, Real.dist_eq, h w (hwx ▸ hδr), hwx] at this
    exact lt_irrefl _ this
  rcases le_total x z with hxz | hzx'
  · have hzx2 : x + δ ≤ z := by
      rw [abs_of_nonneg (by linarith)] at hzx; linarith
    exact key (x + δ) (hord.out hxC hz ⟨by linarith, hzx2⟩) (by
      rw [show x + δ - x = δ by ring, abs_of_pos hδpos])
  · have hzx2 : z ≤ x - δ := by
      rw [abs_of_nonpos (by linarith)] at hzx; linarith
    exact key (x - δ) (hord.out hz hxC ⟨hzx2, by linarith⟩) (by
      rw [show x - δ - x = -δ by ring, abs_neg, abs_of_pos hδpos])

/-- An even map is injective on no neighbourhood of `0`. -/
theorem not_injOn_of_even {f : ℝ → ℝ} (hf : ∀ z, f (-z) = f z) {V : Set ℝ} (hV : IsOpen V)
    (h0 : (0 : ℝ) ∈ V) : ¬ InjOn f V := by
  intro hinj
  obtain ⟨ε, hε, hεV⟩ := Metric.isOpen_iff.1 hV 0 h0
  have h1 : ε / 2 ∈ V := hεV (by
    rw [Metric.mem_ball, Real.dist_eq, sub_zero, abs_of_pos (by positivity)]; linarith)
  have h2 : -(ε / 2) ∈ V := hεV (by
    rw [Metric.mem_ball, Real.dist_eq, sub_zero, abs_neg, abs_of_pos (by positivity)]; linarith)
  have := hinj h1 h2 (hf (ε / 2)).symm
  linarith

/-! ### `rem:ordinary_locii_open_but`: the ordinary loci need not be connected -/

theorem isSpread_abs : IsSpread (fun x : ℝ => |x|) := isLocDistPres_abs.isSpread

theorem zero_notMem_ordY_abs : (0 : ℝ) ∉ ordY (fun x : ℝ => |x|) := by
  have := notMem_ordY_of_forall_not_injOn (p := fun x : ℝ => |x|) continuous_abs (x := 0)
    fun V hV h0 => not_injOn_of_even (fun z => abs_neg z) hV h0
  simpa using this

theorem neg_one_mem_ordY_abs : (-1 : ℝ) ∈ ordY (fun x : ℝ => |x|) := by
  refine subset_ordY_of_preimage_eq_empty (U := Iio 0) isOpen_Iio ?_ (by norm_num : (-1:ℝ) < 0)
  ext x; simp only [mem_preimage, mem_Iio, mem_empty_iff_false, iff_false, not_lt]
  exact abs_nonneg x

/-- The homeomorphism `(-∞, 0) ≃ₜ (0, ∞)`, `z ↦ -z`. -/
def negIioIoi : (Iio (0 : ℝ)) ≃ₜ (Ioi (0 : ℝ)) where
  toFun z := ⟨-z, show (0 : ℝ) < -(z : ℝ) from neg_pos.2 z.2⟩
  invFun z := ⟨-z, show -(z : ℝ) < 0 from neg_lt_zero.2 z.2⟩
  left_inv z := by simp
  right_inv z := by simp
  continuous_toFun := (continuous_neg.comp continuous_subtype_val).subtype_mk _
  continuous_invFun := (continuous_neg.comp continuous_subtype_val).subtype_mk _

@[simp] theorem negIioIoi_apply (z : Iio (0 : ℝ)) : (negIioIoi z : ℝ) = -z := rfl

theorem one_mem_ordY_abs : (1 : ℝ) ∈ ordY (fun x : ℝ => |x|) := by
  refine ⟨Ioi 0, isOpen_Ioi, by norm_num, ?_⟩
  let S : Bool → Set ℝ := fun b => Bool.rec (Iio 0) (Ioi 0) b
  refine isEvenlyCoveredSet_of_sheets S (fun b => ?_) (fun b => ?_) ?_ ?_ (fun b => ?_)
  · cases b
    · exact isOpen_Iio
    · exact isOpen_Ioi
  · cases b
    · exact isPreconnected_Iio
    · exact isPreconnected_Ioi
  · intro b c hbc
    cases b <;> cases c
    · exact absurd rfl hbc
    · show Disjoint (Iio (0:ℝ)) (Ioi 0)
      exact Set.disjoint_left.2 fun x (hx : x < 0) (hx' : 0 < x) => lt_asymm hx hx'
    · show Disjoint (Ioi (0:ℝ)) (Iio 0)
      exact Set.disjoint_left.2 fun x (hx : 0 < x) (hx' : x < 0) => lt_asymm hx hx'
    · exact absurd rfl hbc
  · ext x
    simp only [mem_preimage, mem_Ioi, abs_pos, mem_iUnion, S]
    constructor
    · intro hx
      rcases hx.lt_or_gt with h | h
      · exact ⟨false, h⟩
      · exact ⟨true, h⟩
    · rintro ⟨b, hb⟩
      cases b
      · exact (show x < 0 from hb).ne
      · exact (show 0 < x from hb).ne'
  · cases b
    · exact ⟨negIioIoi, fun z => by rw [negIioIoi_apply]; exact (abs_of_neg z.2).symm⟩
    · exact ⟨Homeomorph.refl _, fun z => (abs_of_pos (z.2 : (0:ℝ) < z)).symm⟩

/-- `rem:ordinary_locii_open_but`, "may not be connected": for the spread `x ↦ |x|` on `ℝ`,
neither ordinary locus is connected. -/
theorem not_isPreconnected_ordY_abs : ¬ IsPreconnected (ordY (fun x : ℝ => |x|)) := by
  rw [isPreconnected_iff_ordConnected]
  intro h
  exact zero_notMem_ordY_abs (h.out neg_one_mem_ordY_abs one_mem_ordY_abs ⟨by norm_num, by norm_num⟩)

theorem not_isPreconnected_ordX_abs : ¬ IsPreconnected (ordX (fun x : ℝ => |x|)) := by
  rw [isPreconnected_iff_ordConnected]
  intro h
  have h1 : (1 : ℝ) ∈ ordX (fun x : ℝ => |x|) := by
    rw [mem_ordX]; simpa using one_mem_ordY_abs
  have h2 : (-1 : ℝ) ∈ ordX (fun x : ℝ => |x|) := by
    rw [mem_ordX]; simpa using one_mem_ordY_abs
  have h0 := h.out h2 h1 ⟨by norm_num, by norm_num⟩ (a := 0)
  exact zero_notMem_ordY_abs (by simpa [mem_ordX] using h0)


/-! ### `rem:ordinary_locii_open_but`: surjectivity of `ord(X) → ord(Y)` -/

/-- The constant map `Unit → Bool` with value `true`. -/
def unitTrue : Unit → Bool := fun _ => true

theorem isSpread_unitTrue : IsSpread unitTrue := by
  refine isSpread_iff_of_locallyConnectedSpace.2 ⟨continuous_of_discreteTopology, ?_⟩
  intro x O _ hxO
  refine ⟨univ, isOpen_univ, mem_univ _, fun z _ => ?_⟩
  rwa [Subsingleton.elim z x]

theorem ordY_unitTrue : ordY unitTrue = univ := by
  refine eq_univ_of_forall fun b => ?_
  cases b
  · refine subset_ordY_of_preimage_eq_empty (U := {false}) (isOpen_discrete _) ?_ rfl
    ext x; simp [unitTrue]
  · refine ⟨{true}, isOpen_discrete _, rfl, fun x hx => ?_⟩
    refine ⟨{ toFun := fun _ => ⟨true, rfl⟩
              invFun := fun _ => ⟨x, mem_connectedComponentIn hx⟩
              left_inv := fun a => Subsingleton.elim _ _
              right_inv := fun b => Subsingleton.elim _ _
              continuous_toFun := continuous_of_discreteTopology
              continuous_invFun := continuous_of_discreteTopology }, fun z => rfl⟩

theorem ordX_unitTrue : ordX unitTrue = univ := by
  rw [ordX, ordY_unitTrue, preimage_univ]

/-- `rem:ordinary_locii_open_but`: with the paper's (vacuous) evenly-covered condition,
`ord(X)` may be connected while `ord(X) → ord(Y)` misses a point of `ord(Y)`; so if "covering"
includes surjectivity, connectedness of `ord(X)` is not the only obstruction (cf.
`surjective_restrict_ordX` for a surjective `p`). -/
theorem unitTrue_counterexample :
    IsSpread unitTrue ∧ IsConnected (ordX unitTrue) ∧
      IsCoveringMap ((ordY unitTrue).restrictPreimage unitTrue) ∧
      ¬ Function.Surjective ((ordY unitTrue).restrictPreimage unitTrue) := by
  refine ⟨isSpread_unitTrue, ?_, isCoveringMap_restrict_ordX continuous_of_discreteTopology, ?_⟩
  · rw [ordX_unitTrue]; exact isConnected_univ
  · intro h
    obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := h ⟨false, by rw [ordY_unitTrue]; exact mem_univ _⟩
    have := congrArg Subtype.val hx
    simp [Set.restrictPreimage, unitTrue] at this

/-! ### `cex:openess` -/

/-- The inclusion `ℝ → ℝ², x ↦ (x, 0)` of `cex:openess`. -/
def lineIncl : ℝ → ℝ × ℝ := fun x => (x, 0)

theorem isEmbedding_lineIncl : IsEmbedding lineIncl :=
  ⟨isInducing_prodMkLeft 0, fun _ _ h => congrArg Prod.fst h⟩

theorem range_lineIncl : range lineIncl = {q : ℝ × ℝ | q.2 = 0} := by
  ext q
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨x, rfl⟩; rfl
  · intro hq; exact ⟨q.1, Prod.ext rfl hq.symm⟩

theorem isClosed_range_lineIncl : IsClosed (range lineIncl) := by
  rw [range_lineIncl]; exact isClosed_eq continuous_snd continuous_const

theorem isSpread_lineIncl : IsSpread lineIncl :=
  IsSpread.of_isInducing isEmbedding_lineIncl.isInducing

theorem not_isOpen_range_lineIncl : ¬ IsOpen (range lineIncl) := by
  intro h
  obtain ⟨ε, hε, hball⟩ := Metric.isOpen_iff.1 h (0, 0) ⟨0, rfl⟩
  have hmem : ((0 : ℝ), ε / 2) ∈ Metric.ball ((0 : ℝ), (0 : ℝ)) ε := by
    rw [Metric.mem_ball, Prod.dist_eq]
    simp only [dist_self, Real.dist_eq, sub_zero]
    rw [abs_of_pos (by positivity)]
    exact max_lt hε (by linarith)
  obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := hball hmem
  have := congrArg Prod.snd hx
  simp [lineIncl] at this
  linarith

/-- `cex:openess`, the correct computation: `ord(Y) = Y ∖ p(X)`. -/
theorem ordY_lineIncl : ordY lineIncl = (range lineIncl)ᶜ := by
  apply subset_antisymm
  · rintro y ⟨U, hU, hyU, hcov⟩ ⟨x, rfl⟩
    have hx : x ∈ lineIncl ⁻¹' U := hyU
    have himg := hcov.image_eq hx
    have hnhds : {t : ℝ | (x, t) ∈ U} ∈ 𝓝 (0 : ℝ) :=
      (Continuous.prodMk_right x).continuousAt.preimage_mem_nhds (hU.mem_nhds hyU)
    obtain ⟨ε, hε, hball⟩ := Metric.mem_nhds_iff.1 hnhds
    have hmem : (x, ε / 2) ∈ U := hball (by
      rw [Metric.mem_ball, Real.dist_eq, sub_zero, abs_of_pos (by positivity)]; linarith)
    rw [← himg] at hmem
    obtain ⟨z, -, hz⟩ := hmem
    have := congrArg Prod.snd hz
    simp [lineIncl] at this
    linarith
  · rw [← isClosed_range_lineIncl.closure_eq]
    exact compl_closure_range_subset_ordY

theorem ordX_lineIncl : ordX lineIncl = ∅ := by
  ext x
  simp [ordX, ordY_lineIncl]

theorem mapsTo_lineIncl : MapsTo lineIncl univ (range lineIncl) := fun x _ => mem_range_self x

/-- The restriction `ℝ = X₁ → Y₁ = p(X)` is a homeomorphism, hence a covering map. -/
theorem isCoveringMap_lineIncl_restrict :
    IsCoveringMap (MapsTo.restrict lineIncl univ (range lineIncl) mapsTo_lineIncl) := by
  have : (MapsTo.restrict lineIncl univ (range lineIncl) mapsTo_lineIncl) =
      ((Homeomorph.Set.univ ℝ).trans isEmbedding_lineIncl.toHomeomorph) := by
    funext x; rfl
  rw [this]
  exact isCoveringMap_of_homeomorph _

/-- `cex:openess`. For the inclusion `ℝ → ℝ²` (a spread) and `X₁ = ℝ` (portly), `Y₁ = p(X)`,
the restriction `X₁ → Y₁` is a covering map but `Y₁` is not open, and every conclusion of
`lem:spread_partial_covering` fails: `Y₁ ∩ ord(Y) = ∅` and `ord(X) = ∅`. The paper's
"`ord(Y) = ∅`" is false as written: `ord(Y) = Y ∖ p(X)` (`ordY_lineIncl`). -/
theorem cex_openess :
    IsSpread lineIncl ∧ IsPortly (univ : Set ℝ) ∧
      IsCoveringMap (MapsTo.restrict lineIncl univ (range lineIncl) mapsTo_lineIncl) ∧
      ¬ IsOpen (range lineIncl) ∧ Disjoint (range lineIncl) (ordY lineIncl) ∧
      ordX lineIncl = ∅ ∧ ¬ (range lineIncl ⊆ ordY lineIncl) ∧ (ordY lineIncl).Nonempty := by
  refine ⟨isSpread_lineIncl, isPortly_univ, isCoveringMap_lineIncl_restrict,
    not_isOpen_range_lineIncl, ?_, ordX_lineIncl, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [ordY_lineIncl]; exact disjoint_compl_right
  · intro h
    have := h ⟨0, rfl⟩
    rw [ordY_lineIncl] at this
    exact this ⟨0, rfl⟩
  · refine ⟨(0, 1), ?_⟩
    rw [ordY_lineIncl, range_lineIncl]
    simp


/-! ### `cex:portlyness`, second item: without density of `X₁` -/

/-- The zigzag `x ↦ ||x| - 1|` on `ℝ`: slopes `± 1`, folds at `-1, 0, 1`. -/
def zigzag : ℝ → ℝ := fun x => |(|x| - 1)|

theorem isLocDistPres_zigzag : IsLocDistPres zigzag :=
  (isLocDistPres_abs.comp (isLocDistPres_sub_const 1)).comp isLocDistPres_abs

theorem isSpread_zigzag : IsSpread zigzag := isLocDistPres_zigzag.isSpread

theorem zigzag_neg (z : ℝ) : zigzag (-z) = zigzag z := by simp [zigzag, abs_neg]

theorem zigzag_zero : zigzag 0 = 1 := by norm_num [zigzag]

theorem zigzag_of_one_lt {x : ℝ} (hx : 1 < x) : zigzag x = x - 1 := by
  simp only [zigzag]
  rw [abs_of_pos (show (0:ℝ) < x by linarith), abs_of_pos (by linarith)]

/-- `1 = zigzag 0` is a fold value: it is not ordinary. -/
theorem one_notMem_ordY_zigzag : (1 : ℝ) ∉ ordY zigzag := by
  have := notMem_ordY_of_forall_not_injOn (p := zigzag) isLocDistPres_zigzag.continuous
    (x := 0) fun V hV h0 => not_injOn_of_even zigzag_neg hV h0
  rwa [zigzag_zero] at this

theorem mapsTo_zigzag : MapsTo zigzag (Ioi 1) (Ioi 0) := fun x (hx : 1 < x) => by
  show 0 < zigzag x
  rw [zigzag_of_one_lt hx]; linarith

/-- The homeomorphism `(1, ∞) ≃ₜ (0, ∞)`, `x ↦ x - 1`. -/
def shiftIoi : (Ioi (1 : ℝ)) ≃ₜ (Ioi (0 : ℝ)) where
  toFun z := ⟨z - 1, show (0 : ℝ) < z - 1 by have : (1 : ℝ) < z := z.2; linarith⟩
  invFun z := ⟨z + 1, show (1 : ℝ) < z + 1 by have : (0 : ℝ) < z := z.2; linarith⟩
  left_inv z := by ext; simp
  right_inv z := by ext; simp
  continuous_toFun := ((continuous_sub_right 1).comp continuous_subtype_val).subtype_mk _
  continuous_invFun := ((continuous_add_const 1).comp continuous_subtype_val).subtype_mk _

theorem isCoveringMap_zigzag_restrict :
    IsCoveringMap (MapsTo.restrict zigzag (Ioi 1) (Ioi 0) mapsTo_zigzag) := by
  have : MapsTo.restrict zigzag (Ioi 1) (Ioi 0) mapsTo_zigzag = shiftIoi := by
    funext z
    exact Subtype.ext (zigzag_of_one_lt z.2)
  rw [this]
  exact isCoveringMap_of_homeomorph _

theorem isLocallyConnectedIn_Ioi_one : IsLocallyConnectedIn (Ioi (1 : ℝ)) := by
  intro W _ hW
  rw [isPreconnected_iff_ordConnected] at hW ⊢
  exact hW.inter ordConnected_Ioi

theorem not_dense_Ioi_one : ¬ Dense (Ioi (1 : ℝ)) := by
  intro h
  have := h.closure_eq
  rw [closure_Ioi] at this
  have h0 : (0 : ℝ) ∈ Ici (1 : ℝ) := this ▸ mem_univ 0
  exact absurd (h0 : (1 : ℝ) ≤ 0) (by norm_num)

/-- `cex:portlyness`, second item, in the strongest true form: a connected, second countable,
locally path-connected Hausdorff `X = ℝ`, a spread `p = zigzag`, `X₁ = (1, ∞)` open and locally
connected in `X` but not dense, `Y₁ = (0, ∞)` open, `X₁ → Y₁` a homeomorphism (hence a covering
map) — and all three conclusions of `lem:spread_partial_covering` fail. -/
theorem cex_portlyness :
    IsSpread zigzag ∧ IsOpen (Ioi (1 : ℝ)) ∧ IsLocallyConnectedIn (Ioi (1 : ℝ)) ∧
      ¬ Dense (Ioi (1 : ℝ)) ∧ IsOpen (Ioi (0 : ℝ)) ∧
      IsCoveringMap (MapsTo.restrict zigzag (Ioi 1) (Ioi 0) mapsTo_zigzag) ∧
      ¬ (Ioi (0 : ℝ) ⊆ ordY zigzag) ∧ ¬ (Ioi (1 : ℝ) ⊆ ordX zigzag) ∧
      zigzag ⁻¹' Ioi 0 ≠ Ioi 1 := by
  refine ⟨isSpread_zigzag, isOpen_Ioi, isLocallyConnectedIn_Ioi_one, not_dense_Ioi_one,
    isOpen_Ioi, isCoveringMap_zigzag_restrict, fun h => ?_, fun h => ?_, fun h => ?_⟩
  · exact one_notMem_ordY_zigzag (h (by norm_num : (0 : ℝ) < 1))
  · have h2 := h (by norm_num : (1 : ℝ) < 2)
    rw [mem_ordX, zigzag_of_one_lt (by norm_num)] at h2
    norm_num at h2
    exact one_notMem_ordY_zigzag h2
  · have hm : (-2 : ℝ) ∈ zigzag ⁻¹' Ioi 0 := by
      show 0 < zigzag (-2)
      rw [zigzag_neg, zigzag_of_one_lt (by norm_num)]; norm_num
    rw [h] at hm
    exact absurd (hm : (1 : ℝ) < -2) (by norm_num)

/-! ### The paper's second example: `ord(Y)` is not empty -/

/-- The set `X ⊆ ℝ²` of `cex:portlyness`, second item: the complement of the open unit disc,
together with the rational rays `{λ x | λ ∈ (0,1], ‖x‖ = 1, x ∈ ℚ²}`. -/
def portlyX : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2)) :=
  {x | 1 ≤ ‖x‖} ∪ {y | ∃ l ∈ Ioc (0 : ℝ) 1, ∃ x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2),
    ‖x‖ = 1 ∧ (∀ i, ∃ q : ℚ, x i = q) ∧ y = l • x}

/-- The map `p` of `cex:portlyness`, second item: `x / ‖x‖²` on the closed unit disc, the
identity outside. -/
def portlyInv (x : portlyX) : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2) :=
  if ‖(x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2))‖ ≤ 1 then
    (‖(x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2))‖ ^ 2)⁻¹ • (x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2))
  else x

theorem norm_pos_of_mem_portlyX {x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2)} (hx : x ∈ portlyX) : 0 < ‖x‖ := by
  rcases hx with hx | ⟨l, ⟨hl0, -⟩, v, hv, -, rfl⟩
  · exact lt_of_lt_of_le one_pos hx
  · rw [norm_smul, hv, mul_one, Real.norm_eq_abs, abs_of_pos hl0]; exact hl0

theorem one_le_norm_portlyInv (x : portlyX) : 1 ≤ ‖portlyInv x‖ := by
  have hpos := norm_pos_of_mem_portlyX x.2
  unfold portlyInv
  split_ifs with h
  · rw [norm_smul, norm_inv, norm_pow, norm_norm, pow_two, mul_inv, mul_assoc,
      inv_mul_cancel₀ hpos.ne', mul_one]
    exact one_le_inv_iff₀.2 ⟨hpos, h⟩
  · exact (not_le.1 h).le

/-- `cex:portlyness`, second item: the paper's "`ord(Y) = ∅`" is false as written. Whatever
topology `X` carries, the open unit disc has empty preimage and is therefore (vacuously) in the
ordinary locus. -/
theorem ball_subset_ordY_portlyInv (τ : TopologicalSpace portlyX) :
    Metric.ball (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2)) 1 ⊆ @ordY portlyX _ τ _ portlyInv := by
  refine @subset_ordY_of_preimage_eq_empty portlyX _ τ _ portlyInv _ Metric.isOpen_ball ?_
  ext x
  simp only [mem_preimage, Metric.mem_ball, dist_zero_right, mem_empty_iff_false, iff_false,
    not_lt]
  exact one_le_norm_portlyInv x

theorem ordY_portlyInv_nonempty (τ : TopologicalSpace portlyX) :
    (@ordY portlyX _ τ _ portlyInv).Nonempty :=
  ⟨0, ball_subset_ordY_portlyInv τ (Metric.mem_ball_self one_pos)⟩

end GX
